01:46:52.240 --> 01:46:56.100
 It felt like I was on stage playing in front of a bunch of like cheering bands, except there

01:46:56.100 --> 01:46:57.000
 was no one around me.

01:46:57.000 --> 01:47:00.040
 And I just got addicted to playing flute out here.

01:47:00.240 --> 01:47:08.940
 So one night, um, I'm with my wife and my friend who came out from, uh, LA.

01:47:09.060 --> 01:47:10.740
 He's an, he's a really cool dude.

01:47:10.740 --> 01:47:14.060
 Uh, he has a, uh, I can, I can talk about him later.

01:47:14.160 --> 01:47:17.760
 If I talk about him more, it's going to be most of this conversation.

01:47:18.600 --> 01:47:26.000
 Uh, interestingly enough, uh, he falls, uh, my wife and, and my friend, um, they, they

01:47:26.000 --> 01:47:30.600
 both fall asleep, my friend in his tent, my wife and our vehicle that we're sleeping in.

01:47:31.260 --> 01:47:35.220
 And, uh, it's about two o'clock and I just tell them that I want to stand out here and

01:47:35.220 --> 01:47:39.340
 play with these acoustics and just play flute, um, until I get really tired.

01:47:40.260 --> 01:47:46.020
 And as I'm playing flute, um, someone says, Hey, you know, climb up to the, you know, climb

01:47:46.020 --> 01:47:47.920
 up a little higher, climb up a little higher.

01:47:48.060 --> 01:47:52.180
 You know, along the side of this long, the side of this Rocky mountain, the Rocky

01:47:52.180 --> 01:47:53.400
 mountain is called spy mountain.

01:47:53.400 --> 01:47:59.940
 This is, it's this, um, arrow head shape mountain, um, that you can actually see from

01:47:59.940 --> 01:48:05.060
 Google earth and, um, you can actually see giant rock right next to the, uh, the

01:48:05.060 --> 01:48:06.480
 Northern part of this mountain.

01:48:06.900 --> 01:48:09.900
 So I'm getting higher and higher and higher up on it.

01:48:09.960 --> 01:48:14.620
 And eventually I'm kind of above giant rock, giant rocks, it's about 70 feet.

01:48:15.260 --> 01:48:20.840
 And I'm sitting in between these two, um, spray painted eyes, which is really interesting.

01:48:21.140 --> 01:48:22.140
 I start playing flute.

01:48:23.500 --> 01:48:26.900
 As I'm playing flute, I'm just like, just, it's like Jimi Hendrix flute up there.

01:48:26.900 --> 01:48:29.300
 I'm just going, finding all these like new notes.

01:48:29.300 --> 01:48:34.360
 And I'm hearing the reverberation of the flute and none of my lights are set up to where I'm

01:48:34.360 --> 01:48:37.040
 seeing the voice activation, the sound activation thing.

01:48:37.040 --> 01:48:37.760
 I'm just playing.

01:48:38.800 --> 01:48:44.680
 And at one point I see these two lights along the desert floor, um, in between this one

01:48:44.680 --> 01:48:49.920
 area where there's this hill that's directly North and the small kind of triangle or form

01:48:49.920 --> 01:48:56.240
 of rocks and the, um, which two couple of years later, my wife and I would get married

01:48:56.240 --> 01:48:58.040
 right in front of this train where rocks.

01:48:58.520 --> 01:49:06.500
 Um, but this two lights just moving across the floor, basically.

01:49:07.340 --> 01:49:13.580
 And, and then at one point I'm playing flute, playing flute, playing flute, and they stop.

01:49:13.580 --> 01:49:17.780
 And I'm like, ah, that's must be people listening to my, to my flute playing.

01:49:18.320 --> 01:49:24.680
 And I keep playing and they're moving, you know, faster and faster and faster.

01:49:24.680 --> 01:49:29.320
 A little faster than, than, you know, a human would normally move.

01:49:30.140 --> 01:49:35.820
 And it was interesting because they're moving in the locations where I had some of my sound

01:49:35.820 --> 01:49:38.320
 activated lights, basically where they were flickering.

01:49:38.360 --> 01:49:44.600
 I'm like, oh my God, there's so they've got their, these, these individuals are probably hearing my flute at

01:49:44.600 --> 01:49:47.580
 its loudest point, right in this sort of this area.

01:49:48.420 --> 01:49:57.040
 And, and then at one point they stopped and it's almost as though I realized that those weren't flashlights.

01:49:57.280 --> 01:50:06.180
 Those were like orbs or they were just light floating by itself, basically.

01:50:06.840 --> 01:50:12.660
 And I'm playing, I'm wondering, I'm having these weird thoughts in my head.

01:50:12.660 --> 01:50:15.180
 Still, I still feel like I'm on stage.

01:50:15.180 --> 01:50:16.380
 It's the weirdest thing.

01:50:17.020 --> 01:50:23.000
 I can't really put together like these, there's just, it's almost like I'm having a conversation with these

01:50:23.000 --> 01:50:26.740
 things as I'm playing flute, but I can't transit the conversation.

01:50:26.860 --> 01:50:28.000
 It's almost like, you cool.

01:50:28.120 --> 01:50:28.540
 You cool.

01:50:28.540 --> 01:50:29.200
 Yeah, I'm cool.

01:50:29.200 --> 01:50:29.560
 Cool.

01:50:29.780 --> 01:50:33.160
 It's like, that sort of thing, like a lead singer too, with an audience.

01:50:33.160 --> 01:50:34.000
 It was really interesting.

01:50:34.180 --> 01:50:41.020
 And then at one point I just, I stopped playing flute and I do this, like, I do this kind of like ending

01:50:41.020 --> 01:50:45.500
 piece where I blow really hard into flute and it creates this flare sound.

01:50:45.500 --> 01:50:50.000
 And now as I do that, I'm like, I take a, you know, I just kind of like laugh and take a bow.

01:50:50.220 --> 01:50:54.060
 And then at that exact moment, these two things just shoot up straight into the air.

01:50:54.920 --> 01:51:02.580
 And, um, I am at, at a, at a very stunned state.

01:51:02.580 --> 01:51:07.860
 I realized what I had just seen and I realized what these things probably were.

01:51:08.220 --> 01:51:10.500
 And I feel afraid at that moment.

01:51:10.760 --> 01:51:13.220
 I'm thinking to myself, am I in danger?

01:51:13.740 --> 01:51:18.720
 Did I just FAFO with, with the phenomenon, you know, that I get too comfortable.

01:51:19.260 --> 01:51:20.520
 I was genuinely very afraid.

01:51:21.780 --> 01:51:26.400
 And I remember as I was about to like, just escape and run down the side of the mountain.

01:51:27.180 --> 01:51:32.400
 Um, I just got this overwhelming feeling through me, like, just keep playing, just keep playing.

01:51:33.660 --> 01:51:35.640
 So I sat back down and started playing more.

01:51:35.640 --> 01:51:47.220
 And eventually that sort of like, you know, weird feeling of me, you know, not supposed to be there, not supposed to be playing this, not supposed to be interacting with these things.

01:51:47.220 --> 01:51:48.480
 These things went away.

01:51:48.480 --> 01:51:52.120
 It was almost like, you know, we found each other.

01:51:52.380 --> 01:51:53.500
 What a wonderful experience.

01:51:53.580 --> 01:51:54.200
 Just keep playing.

01:51:54.780 --> 01:51:57.740
 I did not feel as though these things had left.

01:51:57.880 --> 01:52:03.920
 This is probably one of the most benevolent experiences I've had with this phenomenon.

01:52:05.000 --> 01:52:12.440
 Years later, um, around 2020, I went back up to the exact same spot, played flute.

01:52:13.160 --> 01:52:22.080
 Um, and I had all sorts of interesting experiences where, you know, I saw like a type of fox I had never seen before.

01:52:22.080 --> 01:52:30.480
 It was like this weird kind of like shamanistic experience where a fox comes up, listens to my flute playing, sits for a little while, listens to the flute.

01:52:30.560 --> 01:52:34.580
 I stopped playing flute and then the fox looks at its den and goes into it.

01:52:34.580 --> 01:52:37.120
 And I just discovered that I was playing directly in front of it.

01:52:37.580 --> 01:52:50.480
 Um, another time, um, around that same, around that same time, two years later, I'm playing flute and I see these, these things again, and they're on top of Spy Mountain.

01:52:50.480 --> 01:52:59.900
 Um, and they, it was interesting because I, at first I thought they could have been like airplane lights or stars, but each of the stars looked similar to one another.

01:53:00.200 --> 01:53:01.020
 It was really interesting.

01:53:01.120 --> 01:53:06.040
 It was like, well, that, that looks like Venus, but that star looks like Venus, but that star, those aren't stars.

01:53:06.140 --> 01:53:06.740
 Are those planets?

01:53:06.900 --> 01:53:08.540
 Why they, why do they all look like Venus?

01:53:08.740 --> 01:53:09.640
 That's the weirdest thing.

01:53:10.120 --> 01:53:12.420
 And then they started to sort of move slightly.

01:53:13.560 --> 01:53:15.280
 And then the fear came up again.

01:53:16.160 --> 01:53:19.280
 You know, the response of every time it would get close, the fear would kick in.

01:53:19.280 --> 01:53:19.720
 Oh shit.

01:53:19.780 --> 01:53:20.700
 When am I doing something wrong?

01:53:20.780 --> 01:53:21.660
 Am I not supposed to be here?

01:53:21.660 --> 01:53:23.240
 And it was always the same thing.

01:53:23.240 --> 01:53:26.880
 And then that feeling of just like, no, no, no, keep playing, keep playing, keep playing.

01:53:27.520 --> 01:53:29.960
 It was a very interesting experience.

01:53:30.100 --> 01:53:31.000
 Very interesting experience.

01:53:31.080 --> 01:53:38.260
 One that I, I will admit one of the reasons I keep going back to that place over and over again to try and reconnect with it.

01:53:38.620 --> 01:53:43.740
 Um, I, I, I go there every month, I go there, I'm not every month, every year around the same time.

01:53:43.740 --> 01:53:52.500
 Um, strangely enough, I found one of the best flute makers I've ever played with, um, ever played for the slutes and whatnot.

01:53:52.500 --> 01:53:57.900
 It was like 30 miles, uh, 30, sorry, 30 minutes, uh, south of the location.

01:53:57.900 --> 01:53:59.780
 We'd been there like for 20 years.

01:53:59.860 --> 01:54:08.920
 It was really funny, but, um, that's probably one of my, you know, um, nicest experiences that I've had with it.

01:54:09.300 --> 01:54:14.420
 Um, later on, I would read a chapter in a book called, uh, Skinwalkers of the Pentagon.

01:54:14.420 --> 01:54:20.520
 Um, I think it's either chapter eight or chapter nine, the chapter is called blue orbs are not benign.

01:54:21.300 --> 01:54:33.880
 And I read about these things and I realized that, um, you know, there's, there indeed was a certain danger with these plasma things.

01:54:33.880 --> 01:54:37.400
 And it's interesting too, what the, the recent disclosure sort of talks.

01:54:37.400 --> 01:54:48.640
 I, I, once in a while we'll hear, um, you know, somebody, you know, one of the, um, disclosures, I guess you would call them, uh, talking about, you know, UFOs and whatnot.

01:54:48.920 --> 01:54:52.860
 Once in a while, they'll actually bring up the topic of plasma beings.

01:54:53.720 --> 01:54:58.140
 Um, but yeah, there's a, there's a book that literally talks about them, Skinwalkers of the Pentagon.

01:54:58.340 --> 01:54:59.700
 There's one chapter on it.

01:55:00.220 --> 01:55:07.320
 And then going into, uh, to what you were sort of talking about, JT, like not necessarily UFOs, but, you know, the paranormal.

01:55:07.820 --> 01:55:09.160
 That book is all about that.

01:55:09.480 --> 01:55:25.480
 Um, there's, I don't remember really hearing about, no, no, there, I, I think there might've been some mention of craft in that book, but there's definitely a lot of paranormal, you know, quote unquote, sort of, uh, things within that for sure.

01:55:26.040 --> 01:55:33.080
 Um, you know, another, another quick, another quick story about, uh, giant rock.

01:55:33.080 --> 01:55:35.000
 And this is a really interesting one, I'm sure.

01:55:35.000 --> 01:55:42.600
 Uh, another time that we saw, um, one of those light boots or whatnot, it was, um, it's kind of funny.

01:55:42.600 --> 01:55:45.020
 So I was going there in 20, I need to write this down.

01:55:45.200 --> 01:55:46.200
 So it's 2018.

01:55:46.620 --> 01:55:53.980
 Um, so 2017, no, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, I've been going back ever since as much as I can.

01:55:54.160 --> 01:55:55.300
 It's four hours away from me now.

01:55:56.440 --> 01:56:06.180
 Um, but, uh, the really interesting thing about it was in one of the years I went there, my wife had, uh, contracted cancer.

01:56:06.180 --> 01:56:14.260
 She had spindle cell melanoma, strangely enough, her mother had gotten it around the same time, around the same age that my wife was now.

01:56:14.260 --> 01:56:15.640
 And then, and it killed her.

01:56:15.640 --> 01:56:18.440
 So my wife actually thought that she was going to die.

01:56:19.100 --> 01:56:23.640
 Um, so one of the things I remember her telling me was I want to go back to giant rock.

01:56:23.840 --> 01:56:25.740
 I just want to hang out there for a while.

01:56:26.880 --> 01:56:30.820
 So when we got there, um, we got there really late at night.

01:56:30.820 --> 01:56:45.200
 We set everything up, you know, um, and then, you know, we went to sleep and then the next morning we woke up, nothing paranormal, uh, the first night we woke up and my wife wants to, we brought, we brought some friends with us.

01:56:45.200 --> 01:56:56.720
 And my wife wanted to show, um, um, my wife wanted to show, um, our friends, like some of the strange acoustics that are around in that area and stuff.

01:56:56.720 --> 01:56:57.240
 Like that.

01:56:57.300 --> 01:57:01.720
 And then I wanted to like run some acoustic tests in the mountain a little bit.

01:57:01.720 --> 01:57:06.600
 And I was pointing at this one spot, trying to tell my wife, Hey, let's bring everybody over here.

01:57:06.600 --> 01:57:10.880
 And she was like, she's like, uh, yeah, but I want to show everyone this one spot.

01:57:10.880 --> 01:57:18.320
 That's like, you know, right across from, you know, this, the adjacent, you know, sort of spot in the mountain that you're trying to show everybody.

01:57:19.000 --> 01:57:26.560
 And, um, so I, I, I, I climb up, I find like a nice little echoey pervasse within the, I think that's what it's called.

01:57:26.560 --> 01:57:29.080
 Within the, within the side of a spy mountain.

01:57:29.800 --> 01:57:30.600
 She goes down.

01:57:31.240 --> 01:57:39.280
 Um, she, I twist my ankle and she, um, basically says, Hey, I'll come right back up.

01:57:39.280 --> 01:57:46.400
 I'm just going to, uh, take a couple of people back to, back to the, uh, to the tent, but I'll come back up and I'll come for you.

01:57:46.400 --> 01:57:47.200
 I said, okay, cool.

01:57:47.720 --> 01:57:48.800
 So four hours go by.

01:57:50.120 --> 01:57:51.160
 She doesn't come back up.

01:57:51.880 --> 01:57:53.680
 And I'm like, what the hell just happened?

01:57:53.680 --> 01:57:54.760
 Why isn't she coming down?

01:57:54.960 --> 01:58:09.080
 And so I'm up there and I'm just, you know, decide, I'm just going to kind of meditate with, uh, with, you know, do a meditation and talk and, and just kind of, you know, play flute and just be with myself.

01:58:09.400 --> 01:58:14.040
 But at the same time, you know, just kind of be like a psycho psychic biometer.

01:58:14.560 --> 01:58:19.160
 So, you know, just kind of write, talk to my camera, talk about my impressions that I'm getting up there.

01:58:19.960 --> 01:58:23.360
 Which I did, I vlogged while I was in there and playing flute.

01:58:24.120 --> 01:58:32.160
 And, uh, at, at some point I decided to take my, one of my tripods and make it into a cane and I go down the mountain.

01:58:32.840 --> 01:58:40.320
 And as I get to the camping spot, um, I noticed that the car that we drove in, all the doors are open.

01:58:40.880 --> 01:58:42.840
 The tr the back truck is open.

01:58:43.240 --> 01:58:46.480
 The cooler that we have is tipped over, open.

01:58:47.000 --> 01:58:49.520
 Um, there's ice all over the sand.

01:58:49.680 --> 01:58:53.520
 So I put that back up and then all of the doors.

01:58:53.560 --> 01:58:56.360
 All the doors to the tents that are open.

01:58:57.680 --> 01:59:02.440
 And as I look inside, I see my wife, she's sleeping on her inflatable mattress.

01:59:02.480 --> 01:59:06.920
 My two friends are each sleeping on their own inflatable mattresses.

01:59:07.120 --> 01:59:12.280
 My dog that we brought with us is also sleeping on the inflatable mattress.

01:59:12.760 --> 01:59:16.040
 My wife is on and everyone is dead asleep.

01:59:16.240 --> 01:59:19.640
 I'm like, Hey guys, Hey guys, are you awake?

01:59:20.520 --> 01:59:22.200
 And no one's waking up.

01:59:22.200 --> 01:59:28.440
 And I just kind of grabbed my head and I'm like, you know, looking around to see if there's any other buddy at giant rocket on this plane.

01:59:29.080 --> 01:59:29.880
 There's no one there.

01:59:29.880 --> 01:59:30.600
 It's just us.

01:59:31.160 --> 01:59:36.360
 So I'm thinking someone getting to our stuff, you know, something bad happened or they're just so tired.

01:59:36.360 --> 01:59:38.760
 They fell asleep and they just left all the doors open.

01:59:38.760 --> 01:59:39.960
 It was highly unlikely.

01:59:40.600 --> 01:59:43.080
 I mean, especially for my wife, but that's not her.

01:59:43.080 --> 01:59:44.680
 She checks the doors.

01:59:44.680 --> 01:59:45.880
 She locks everything.

01:59:45.880 --> 01:59:52.680
 She's really, really, really, really careful, extra paranoid too, about like, you know, people just coming into our campsite, stealing stuff.

01:59:52.680 --> 01:59:54.360
 So she, she locks everything down.

01:59:54.360 --> 01:59:57.480
 She's better at security than, than most people I know.

01:59:58.040 --> 02:00:02.600
 And just everyone is completely dead asleep.

02:00:03.000 --> 02:00:04.840
 At one point, I'm trying to wake people up.

02:00:04.840 --> 02:00:05.560
 They can't wake up.

02:00:06.280 --> 02:00:13.720
 I pick up my dog and I, uh, I walk with her and like about maybe a hundred feet away from the camp spot.

02:00:13.720 --> 02:00:15.800
 And she begins to wake up a little bit.

02:00:15.800 --> 02:00:16.920
 She's waking up more and more.

02:00:17.960 --> 02:00:22.760
 And I put her down and she pees like a spot, like about a few feet from me.

02:00:22.760 --> 02:00:32.440
 And then she looks at me and then she looks at the camp spot and she goes back and sits back up on the, um, on the, uh, on the, uh, inflatable mattress and falls asleep.

02:00:33.400 --> 02:00:37.640
 And I'm trying to scratch my head, like what's going on?

02:00:37.640 --> 02:00:39.080
 Why is everyone just dead asleep?

02:00:39.080 --> 02:00:40.440
 Why, why aren't they getting up?

02:00:40.440 --> 02:00:44.760
 Eventually, like a couple hours later, people gradually begin to wake up.

02:00:45.320 --> 02:00:49.640
 My, my, my two friends wake up, but my wife is still having some issues.

02:00:49.640 --> 02:00:51.000
 She can't wake up.

02:00:51.000 --> 02:00:52.760
 She just wants to sleep.

02:00:52.760 --> 02:00:57.800
 And she's almost, it's almost like she's experiencing, you know, alcohol poisoning or a hangover.

02:00:58.360 --> 02:01:00.680
 She's like, she's just, just, she's not doing good.

02:01:01.320 --> 02:01:05.560
 So I asked her if she wants to leave and she's like, no, no, I just want to rest a little bit.

02:01:05.560 --> 02:01:06.760
 I'll, I'll get up in a little while.

02:01:07.480 --> 02:01:13.640
 And I, I kind of put my head next to her for a little bit, you know, just kind of petting her head.

02:01:13.640 --> 02:01:17.960
 And I begin to notice that I'm sort of longing to sleep a little bit as I put my head down.

02:01:17.960 --> 02:01:19.560
 I'm like, I don't know if I want to experience that.

02:01:19.560 --> 02:01:26.680
 So I stood up and I'm like, I'm going to, I'm going to start packing everything up and took a while.

02:01:26.680 --> 02:01:34.440
 And then at one point I took a break and I went out, played flute, walked around, explored, did some acoustic tests, came back.

02:01:35.960 --> 02:01:43.320
 Night comes over the camp spot where we're loading the last of the stuff onto, into her car.

02:01:43.320 --> 02:01:48.040
 And at this point, both of my friends are helping run everything up, night, night's coming.

02:01:49.000 --> 02:01:50.440
 My wife is still down asleep though.

02:01:50.840 --> 02:01:51.880
 She's having a hard time.

02:01:52.840 --> 02:01:53.800
 Interestingly enough.

02:01:54.920 --> 02:01:58.280
 One thing I forgot to mention within that four hours, when I was in that crevasse.

02:01:58.280 --> 02:02:00.840
 One of the things I did when I was meditating was I prayed.

02:02:01.560 --> 02:02:05.480
 I prayed for my wife's miraculous healing.

02:02:05.480 --> 02:02:06.920
 I knew what was at stake.

02:02:06.920 --> 02:02:09.000
 I knew she had spindle cell melanoma.

02:02:09.000 --> 02:02:12.680
 I knew it was something that had killed her, killed her mom.

02:02:12.680 --> 02:02:16.440
 You know, she lost her mom when she was 12, sadly, to spindle cell melanoma.

02:02:17.240 --> 02:02:20.120
 And I didn't, you know, of course I didn't want to lose her.

02:02:20.760 --> 02:02:27.080
 She lost her mom, but at the same time, I really wanted her to have hope that she could beat this thing.

02:02:27.720 --> 02:02:32.680
 And so I prayed, I prayed that, you know, she would get better.

02:02:33.560 --> 02:02:39.480
 And it was interesting because later on that night, as we're loading her up, this drone came over.

02:02:40.120 --> 02:02:45.560
 And one of the first time I ever saw like a large drone that moved silently.

02:02:45.560 --> 02:02:47.640
 You could see lights coming off of it.

02:02:47.640 --> 02:02:50.440
 I assumed it was a commercial drone of some sort.

02:02:52.120 --> 02:02:57.720
 And it just kind of stood over us as I was, as I picked my wife up, scooped her up and put her in

02:02:57.720 --> 02:02:58.600
 the passenger seat.

02:02:59.080 --> 02:03:00.600
 And she still didn't feel well.

02:03:00.600 --> 02:03:01.800
 And she was still, you know,

02:03:02.440 --> 02:03:04.120
 um, half asleep.

02:03:04.120 --> 02:03:11.000
 Um, and, uh, at one point I told everybody and was going to my friend say, everyone look up.

02:03:11.560 --> 02:03:13.720
 Don't, don't, don't do anything weird.

02:03:13.720 --> 02:03:15.400
 Just, just, just observe it.

02:03:15.400 --> 02:03:17.000
 And we're observing it.

02:03:17.000 --> 02:03:18.040
 We're not giving it a show.

02:03:18.840 --> 02:03:21.800
